---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Terms of Service - Solar Calculator India";
const description = "Terms of Service and Conditions of Use for SolarCalculatorIndia.com. Independent rooftop solar utility simulation platform.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
      
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 font-display mb-4">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mb-8">
        Last Updated: November 8, 2026
      </p>

      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-slate-600 space-y-4 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          By accessing and using <strong>SolarCalculatorIndia.com</strong> (the "Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you disagree with any part of these terms, please do not use our website.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 pt-3">1. Nature of the Service</h3>
        <p>
          SolarCalculatorIndia.com provides free simulation models, estimates, and informational calculators for residential and commercial rooftop solar feasibility. All estimations regarding system capacity (kW), roof area, benchmark equipment costs, government subsidies, and savings are generated for educational and preliminary planning purposes.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 pt-3">2. No Commercial Warranty / Site Inspection Mandatory</h3>
        <p>
          Actual electricity generation depends on weather conditions, seasonal solar irradiance, roof orientation (tilt angle and azimuth), shading from surrounding trees or buildings, and specific inverter efficiency. Actual turnkey project costs and central subsidy disbursements are strictly subject to technical site survey by an empaneled solar installer and formal sanction by your local DISCOM and the Ministry of New and Renewable Energy (MNRE).
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 pt-3">3. Non-Governmental Entity Notice</h3>
        <p>
          SolarCalculatorIndia.com is a private, non-governmental tool. We do not represent, act as an agent for, or disburse government funds on behalf of the Government of India or any state electricity utility. To register for official government subsidy benefits under the PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana, users must apply directly at the official portal: https://pmsuryaghar.gov.in.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 pt-3">4. Intellectual Property</h3>
        <p>
          The layout, code, interactive calculator logic, visual designs, and original editorial content on SolarCalculatorIndia.com are the exclusive intellectual property of the platform and protected under copyright laws.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
